# f1 = cut. The key is held below the length, the length is stored over, and the element is read. The store ends what the walk knows of the length: the read asks for itself and finds nothing behind the new end.
# Fault injection, testing=IgnoreLengthStores: the walk assumes that the read is in bounds because of the test before the store.
# No run with the fault alone is stored, because it would read past the end of the array.
# With --aot-harden=ignore-told-ranges (testing=CheckBoundsAtRunTime), the read checks its index against the length. If the check fails, the process crashes with a named error.
# AS-USERS-BUILD: under the checks of the runner the verifier of the code refuses the lie at the read (walk/a-length-written-between-the-ground-of-an-access-and-the-access-is-refused.ir): what the emitters hold under the words is asked without them
